Exercise: sa-nfs-review (chapter 19 lab)

serverb is the NFS server and servera is the client. Work with sudo or as
root. The user student exists on both machines.

On serverb
 1. Create /srv/projects, owned by student, and /srv/archive/2025 with a file
    notes.txt in it. Install nfs-utils on both machines if needed.
 2. Export /srv/projects read-write and /srv/archive read-only to your lab
    network (172.25.250.0/24 on the course network, whatever your lab uses).
 3. Start and enable nfs-server and open the nfs service in the firewall,
    permanently.

On servera
 4. Mount serverb:/srv/projects on /mnt/projects permanently through
    /etc/fstab, with the option _netdev. Test with mount -a.
 5. As student, write the line "written from servera" into
    /mnt/projects/from-client.txt. It must be owned by student on serverb.
 6. Install autofs, enable it, and make /remote/archive serve every
    directory of serverb:/srv/archive read-only on demand:
      /etc/auto.master.d/archive.autofs  and  /etc/auto.archive
    (a wildcard map). Test by listing /remote/archive/2025.

On workstation
 7. Fill in answers.txt.

Then, on workstation:  lab grade sa-nfs-review
